## Training

| | |
| --- | --- |
| strategy | dspark (online, disaggregated managed-local) |
| epochs | **12** -> 129,173 optimizer steps = (1,420,909 x 12) // 132 |
| global batch | 132 = batch_size 2 x accumulation_steps 11 x 6 trainer ranks (same as the dense arm; the published run used 128 on 32 ranks) |
| steps per epoch | 10,764.5 -> checkpoint every 10,764 steps, all kept: epoch k = `<run_id>-step{10764 k}` |
| optimizer | AdamW, fp32 master params, weight_decay 0 |
| lr / schedule | 6e-4, cosine over all 129,173 steps, warmup 4% |
| max_grad_norm | 1.0 |
| num_anchors / loss_decay_gamma / objective_chunk_blocks | 512 / 7.0 / 128 |
| loss | 0.1 CE + 0.9 L1, confidence loss 0 |
| attention_backend | flex_attention |
| sharding / dtype / kernels | NO_SHARD (DDP) / bf16 / Liger |
| seed / prompt_seed | 42 / 42 |
| log_interval | 10 |

## Deployment (8x H200, `deployment.mode: disaggregated`, managed_local)

| | |
| --- | --- |
| capture servers | 2 x SGLang TP1 bf16 (`--spec-capture-method dspark`), GPUs 0-1, ports 30000-30001, `sglang_context_length` 8208, `max_running_requests` 4, `max_total_tokens` 65536, radix cache off, triton attention |
| trainer ranks | 6 x DDP, GPUs 2-7 |
| feature transport | Mooncake (tcp), 100 GiB segment, in-flight watermarks 132 / 264 samples, resident 120 / 200 GiB |
| launch | `WANDB_RUN_ID=dense-1-8 WANDB_RESUME=allow specforge train -c <yaml> model.target_model_path=/scratch/models/Qwen3-8B data.train_data_path=/scratch/data/perfectblend/...jsonl data.cache_dir=/scratch/cache/qwen3-8b-dspark-perfectblend-8192 output_dir=/scratch/outputs/<run_id> deployment.disaggregated.control_dir=/scratch/outputs/<run_id>/control tracking.wandb_dir=/scratch/outputs/<run_id>/wandb` |

Also on this branch: the `--nccl-port` pin for managed-local capture servers
(`specforge/launch_plan.py`), so two servers started in the same second cannot
collide on the torch.distributed TCPStore port.

